# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# DDLSmith
#
# Tracked on purpose (do NOT add rules for these):
#   src/, docs/            sources, the design/ER/acceptance documents, and the
#                          research probes under docs/er_features/
#   bugs/                  the curated defect reports: one file per distinct
#                          defect plus bugs/INDEX.md. This is a result, not a
#                          by-product, so it is versioned even though runs
#                          accumulate into it.
#   config.json            the default connection settings the README documents
#   runs/*.ps1             the acceptance-campaign harness scripts (Windows)
#   runs/*.sh              the same harness for Linux; run-category.sh and
#                          run-category.ps1 are meant to be read side by side
#   runs/*.py              harness helpers with no shell equivalent (reading the
#                          resource sampler's output)
#   runs/*.md              the campaign reports: what a run found and what was
#                          changed in response. A result, like bugs/, so it is
#                          versioned even though the tree it describes is not.
#   runs/*.txt             the replay inputs: the "Reproduce this run" command of
#                          every failure a campaign filed, one per line. Their
#                          jars and logs are scratch and stay ignored.
#   runs/*.sql             the verification fixtures: the bare-SQL reproductions
#                          and A/B probes that confirm or refute what a campaign
#                          reported. A result, like runs/*.md, and useless as a
#                          shell script because it has to be pasted verbatim.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- Build output ----------------------------------------------------------
target/
*.class
dependency-reduced-pom.xml

# --- Run output ------------------------------------------------------------
# Failure logs and --log-each-select traces.
logs/

# Campaign scratch space: one directory per acceptance round, each holding its
# chunk logs, per-chunk bug directories and the embedded databases it created.
# Hundreds of MB per round, all of it regenerable from a seed.
# The harness scripts that drive the rounds sit at the top level and are kept.
runs/*
!runs/*.ps1
!runs/*.sh
!runs/*.py
!runs/*.md
!runs/*.txt
!runs/*.sql

# Every generated DDL script (--ddl-dump-dir) and exported ER diagram.
*-ddl-dump/
*.ddl-dump/

# --- Embedded databases ----------------------------------------------------
# SQLite *.db, DuckDB *.duckdb, H2 *.mv.db / *.trace.db, plus their journals.
*.db
*.duckdb
*.db-journal
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
*.duckdb.wal

# --- Logs ------------------------------------------------------------------
*.log
hs_err_pid*.log
replay_pid*.log

# --- IDE / editor ----------------------------------------------------------
.idea/
*.iml
*.ipr
*.iws
.vscode/
.settings/
.classpath
.project
.factorypath
*.swp
*~

# --- OS --------------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
Desktop.ini
$RECYCLE.BIN/

# --- Python (the research scripts under docs/er_features) ------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
